hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2828","**\nNarrated to us Ar-Rabee' ibn Sulaymaan, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who informed me Maalik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu'n-Nadr, on the authority of 'Umayr, the freed slave of Ibn 'Abbaas, on the authority of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Haarith (RA), that some people disputed in the presence of Umm al-Fadl (RA) on the Day of 'Arafah regarding whether the Messenger of Allaah (ﷺ) was fasting or not. Some of them said, \He is fasting","\"" and others said"," \""He is not fasting.\"" So Umm al-Fadl (RA) sent him a cup of milk while he was standing on his camel"," and he drank it that day at 'Arafah.\n\nNarrated to us Ar-Rabee' ibn Sulaymaan"," narrated to us Ibn Wahb"," who informed me 'Amr ibn al-Haarith"," on the authority of Abu'n-Nadr"," on the authority of 'Umayr"," on the authority of Umm al-Fadl (RA)"," with the same narration."""
"2829","Narrated to us Al-Rabee’, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, he informed me ‘Amr, on the authority of Bukayr, from Kuraib, the freed slave of Ibn ‘Abbaas, from Maimoonah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with the same narration.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
